{"parentUuid":"a27932e9-38c5-4a47-a3d4-a49c20053408","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08abe0c37f20c6b8","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JDZJkCryC8sSpxgTSTgAoG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BCWSKt2JqhQTy8tZLLesUy","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"OR-Tools \"lb_tree_search\" subsolver UNSAT proof learning"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7188,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":211,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7188},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":211,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7188,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7188,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caoy7FNL9EymjMod3tpG7","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ca0736fa-983b-4889-a06c-dc6aac3d2b1a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:15.676Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ca0736fa-983b-4889-a06c-dc6aac3d2b1a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a08abe0c37f20c6b8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BCWSKt2JqhQTy8tZLLesUy","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools \"lb_tree_search\" subsolver UNSAT proof learning\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CPMpy ortools interface (cpmpy.solvers.ortools) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/minizinc_installed_subsolver/api/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/tree/stable/ortools/sat\"},{\"title\":\"UnSAT core extraction with assumptions — CPMpy 0.9.23 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/z3-auto-subsolver/unsat_core_extraction.html\"},{\"title\":\"SubSolver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/sat/subsolver/SubSolver\"},{\"title\":\"[2211.12581] UNSAT Solver Synthesis via Monte Carlo Forest Search\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.12581\"},{\"title\":\"Finding the smallest tree in the forest: Monte Carlo Forest Search for UNSAT solving | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=8MneBPDxV9L\"},{\"title\":\"[2401.14996] A Resolution-Based Interactive Proof System for UNSAT\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.14996\"},{\"title\":\"CS 2429 - Propositional Proof Complexity Lecture #2: 19 September 2002\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~toni/Courses/Proofcomplexity/Lectures/Lecture2/lecture2.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Release Notes | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/support/release_notes\"},{\"title\":\"Tutorial #10: SAT Solvers II: Algorithms - Research Blog | RBC Borealis\",\"url\":\"https://rbcborealis.com/research-blogs/tutorial-10-sat-solvers-ii-algorithms/\"}]\n\nThe search results contain information related to OR-Tools and subsolver functionality, as well as UNSAT proof and SAT solving concepts. Here's what I found:\n\n## OR-Tools and Subsolvers\n\nSubSolvers in OR-Tools are used for distributing work, generate tasks via `GenerateTask()`, which are executed in parallel, with `Synchronize()` integrating results from completed tasks and providing identification and search statistics.\n\n## UNSAT Proof Support\n\nOR-Tools includes support for writing UNSAT proofs in the DRAT format, which allows checking the correctness of an UNSAT proof with the third party program DRAT-trim. OR-Tools added a drat writer to check proofs on unsatisfiability.\n\n## Assumptions and UNSAT Cores\n\nLazy Clause Generation solvers like OR-Tools are built on SAT solvers and can inherit the ability to define assumptions and extract an unsatisfiable core, with OR-Tools supporting this since version 8.2.\n\nHowever, the search results do not contain specific information about the `lb_tree_search` subsolver or details about proof learning in that context. The query term \"lb_tree_search\" does not appear in the search results retrieved. If you need more specific information about that particular subsolver component, you may want to check the OR-Tools GitHub repository directly or consult the detailed API documentation for that specific subsolver.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cba464d8-ed61-40d8-b011-21cd1ce887d2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:22.682Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ca0736fa-983b-4889-a06c-dc6aac3d2b1a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a27932e9-38c5-4a47-a3d4-a49c20053408","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a08abe0c37f20c6b8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015JfYqgLZL7FNMK2hWj58bW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT optimize_with_lb_tree_search subsolver OR-Tools sat_parameters proto\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT claims to find optimal solution to a MILP\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/4fcAuWiIUFA\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Custom combination of subsolvers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/pQ4B7QD6ebw\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy ortools interface (cpmpy.solvers.ortools) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/minizinc_installed_subsolver/api/solvers/ortools.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about the CP-SAT `lb_tree_search` subsolver and related OR-Tools sat_parameters:\n\n## lb_tree_search Subsolver\n\nThe `lb_tree_search` subsolver is focused on improving the proven bound, not on finding better solutions. By disproving the feasibility of the cheapest nodes in the search tree, it incrementally improves the bound, but has only little chances to find better solutions.\n\nIn the sat_parameters.proto file, `lb_tree_search` is described as a subsolver \"to improve lower bound, MIP like tree search\".\n\n## Subsolver Context\n\nFull problem subsolvers are solvers that search the full problem space, e.g., by a branch-and-bound algorithm. The `lb_tree_search` is one of 11 full problem subsolvers available in CP-SAT, alongside others like core, default_lp, max_lp, no_lp, objective_lb_search, probing, pseudo_costs, quick_restart, quick_restart_no_lp, and reduced_costs.\n\n## sat_parameters.proto Configuration\n\nThe ortools solver parameters are defined in its 'sat_parameters.proto' description. You can define your own subsolver with a specific configuration, but it is important not to modify the parameters at the top level, as this would affect all subsolvers, including the LNS-workers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"fa2579e6-42a6-42db-9aed-f33eb347d790","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:26.564Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a27932e9-38c5-4a47-a3d4-a49c20053408","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
