{"parentUuid":"4f50b25a-bdbe-4084-a0db-0c883676b56f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a08abe0c37f20c6b8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VHh5JFYQcbJgvBaSrGdn6E","type":"tool_result","content":"# Search Results for lb_tree_search References\n\nBased on the provided content, I found **one reference** to `lb_tree_search`:\n\n## Single Reference Location\n\nIn the multithread subsolver documentation (around line 207), the parameter descriptions mention:\n\n> \"lb_tree_search (to improve lower bound, MIP like tree search)\"\n\nThis appears within a comment listing available subsolver parameter names that can be used in multithread configurations.\n\n## Key Finding\n\n**No proto field definitions exist** in the provided excerpt for `lb_tree_search` or `optimize_with_lb_tree_search`. The reference is descriptive only—indicating this is a named subsolver configuration option rather than a standalone parameter with default values.\n\n## Related Context\n\nThe relevant section discusses:\n- `subsolvers` field (repeated string) for specifying parameter sets\n- `extra_subsolvers` field to add additional worker types\n- `ignore_subsolvers` and `filter_subsolvers` fields using glob patterns\n- `subsolver_params` field for custom subsolver configurations\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe document excerpt does not contain complete field definitions, default values, or activation conditions for `lb_tree_search`. The full proto file extends beyond line 1000 (indicated by the truncation notice), so additional details may exist in the remainder of the file."}]},"uuid":"868a8ca1-d5bb-4bd4-89d8-68e64056a032","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:38.489Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4f50b25a-bdbe-4084-a0db-0c883676b56f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-s