{"parentUuid":"f1c34a27-6394-48c5-8c3d-30d21977d67b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a08abe0c37f20c6b8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HNfwz4DSSokczaLJRDzrDJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"optimize_with_lb_tree_search\" CP-SAT default true false parameter\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT claims to find optimal solution to a MILP\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/4fcAuWiIUFA\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Custom combination of subsolvers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/pQ4B7QD6ebw\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Constraint Programming Solver | google/or-tools | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/google/or-tools/4.1-cp-sat-constraint-programming-solver\"}]\n\nI found some information about the `lb_tree_search` solver in CP-SAT, but I didn't find the specific `optimize_with_lb_tree_search` parameter. Let me search more specifically for that parameter.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cpmpy.solvers.ortools — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/cp_optimizer/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"Binary Search Tree — An Efficient Data Structure | by Abdul Mateen | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@amateen_74225/binary-search-tree-an-efficient-data-structure-36cb7b7a2d4b\"},{\"title\":\"Autumn: A Scalable Read Optimized LSM-tree based Key-Value Stores with Fast Point and Range Read Speed\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2305.05074v2\"},{\"title\":\"Learners · Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://docs.interpretable.ai/stable/OptimalTrees/learner/\"},{\"title\":\"Optimal Binary Search Tree - GeeksforGeeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/dsa/optimal-binary-search-tree-dp-24/\"},{\"title\":\"Balanced Search Trees\",\"url\":\"https://cse.taylor.edu/~jdenning/classes/cos265/slides/11_BalancedSearchTrees.html\"},{\"title\":\"The Power of B-Trees: Optimizing Data Storage and Retrieval | by Nayeem Islam | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@nomannayeem/the-power-of-b-trees-optimizing-data-storage-and-retrieval-a20f0fa05846\"},{\"title\":\"BST (Binary Search Tree) and AVL Tree, Data Structures: (Trees, Part II) - DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/harshm03/bst-binary-search-tree-and-avl-tree-data-structures-trees-part-ii-2lp8\"},{\"title\":\"Red-black Trees (rbtree) in Linux — The Linux Kernel documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/v5.9/core-api/rbtree.html\"},{\"title\":\"Self-Balancing Binary Search Trees | Baeldung on Computer Science\",\"url\":\"https://www.baeldung.com/cs/self-balancing-bts\"}]\n\nGreat! I found relevant information. Let me search for more specific details about this parameter in the official OR-Tools documentation.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"v9.8.3296 How do you log intermediate progress? · google/or-tools · Discussion #3989\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3989\"},{\"title\":\"Release v9.10 (2024/05) · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/releases/tag/v9.10\"},{\"title\":\"v9.10 · google/or-tools · Discussion #4232\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/4232\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/graph/one_tree_lower_bound.h at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/graph/one_tree_lower_bound.h\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/or-tools: Google's Operations Research tools: · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/graph/one_tree_lower_bound.h at master · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/master/ortools/graph/one_tree_lower_bound.h\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/constraint_solver/routing_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/constraint_solver/routing_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"Release v9.13 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/releases/tag/v9.13\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/constraint_solver/constraint_solveri.h at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/constraint_solver/constraint_solveri.h\"}]\n\nPerfect! I found the information. Based on my search results, I can provide you with the details about the `optimize_with_lb_tree_search` parameter in CP-SAT:\n\n## Results\n\nThe parameter `optimize_with_lb_tree_search` in CP-SAT has a default value of `false`. This parameter is marked as experimental.\n\nThe lb_tree_search solver is focused on improving the proven bound, not on finding better solutions. By disproving the feasibility of the cheapest nodes in the search tree, it incrementally improves the bound, but has only little chances to find better solutions.\n\nThis parameter controls whether CP-SAT uses the lower-bound tree search algorithm as part of its optimization strategy, which is primarily oriented toward improving the objective lower bound rather than finding high-quality feasible solutions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"55acbf18-c09d-4e26-a49c-a577608ac6f3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:53.868Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f1c34a27-6394-48c5-8c3d-30d21977d67b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
