{"parentUuid":"6a3600c5-09ea-4a3c-bcea-9518115ec7d3","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08abe0c37f20c6b8","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Pke6SBkmHPfFYMMGZYLYuv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KuNV9dTRqPcqwQGhj23sTq","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/cp_model_search.cc","prompt":"Find references to lb_tree_search subsolver. What conditions activate it by default? How is it added to the subsolvers list? Does it require an objective? Number of workers threshold? Quote relevant code sections."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3739,"cache_read_input_tokens":24460,"output_tokens":424,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3739},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":424,"cache_read_input_tokens":24460,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3739,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3739,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyATXQF5YN6DNQmmT8Y","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"035650f1-60f4-44f0-9eea-ee05702a8a7b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:00.968Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6a3600c5-09ea-4a3c-bcea-9518115ec7d3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a08abe0c37f20c6b8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sv3W2rV6rWBgjeKvDqJuEu","type":"tool_result","content":"# Comment Blocks for LB Tree Search Parameters\n\n## optimize_with_lb_tree_search (lines 2074-2081)\n\n\"Do a more conventional tree search (by opposition to SAT based one) where we keep all the explored node in a tree. This is meant to be used in a portfolio and focus on improving the objective lower bound. Keeping the whole tree allow us to report a better objective lower bound coming from the worst open node in the tree.\"\n\n## save_lp_basis_in_lb_tree_search (lines 2083-2092)\n\n\"Experimental. Save the current LP basis at each node of the search tree so that when we jump around, we can load it and reduce the number of LP iterations needed.\n\nIt currently works okay if we do not change the lp with cuts or simplification... More work is needed to make it robust in all cases.\"\n\n---\n\n**Summary:** The first parameter enables a tree-search strategy that maintains explored nodes to compute tighter objective lower bounds, distinct from SAT-based approaches. The second is an experimental optimization that caches LP basis information across tree nodes to reduce LP solver iterations, though it requires additional robustness work."}]},"uuid":"8787c371-b84e-4e0a-ac88-df05ab2da9bd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:03.651Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6a3600c5-09ea-4a3c-bcea-9518115ec7d3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"035650f1-60f4-44f0-9eea-ee05702a8a7b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a08abe0c37f20c6b8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KuNV9dTRqPcqwQGhj23sTq","type":"tool_result","content":"# lb_tree_search Subsolver Analysis\n\n## Default Activation\n\nThe `lb_tree_search` subsolver is added to the default strategy list unconditionally:\n\n```\nnames.push_back(\"lb_tree_search\");\n```\n\nThis occurs within the section handling empty `subsolvers()` configuration, making it part of the standard worker set.\n\n## Objective Requirement\n\nYes, it requires an objective. The code explicitly filters it out:\n\n```\nif (params.optimize_with_lb_tree_search()) continue;\n```\n\nThis removal happens in the block labeled \"Remove subsolvers that require an objective,\" which executes when `!cp_model.has_objective()`.\n\n## Deterministic Mode Limitation\n\nThe subsolver has a restriction in interleaved/deterministic mode:\n\n```\nif (params.interleave_search() &&\n    (params.optimize_with_lb_tree_search() || ...)) {\n  continue;\n}\n```\n\nThis prevents its use when deterministic behavior is required.\n\n## Configuration Details\n\nThe parameters for `lb_tree_search` disable shared objective bounds and emphasize LP computation:\n\n```\nnew_params.set_optimize_with_lb_tree_search(true);\nnew_params.set_share_objective_bounds(false);\nnew_params.set_root_lp_iterations(100'000);\n```\n\n## Worker Threshold\n\nNo explicit worker count threshold is mentioned for this subsolver's inclusion."}]},"uuid":"d515d3d6-cc76-4aa7-a29e-5d3bec1c97ed","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:05.775Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"035650f1-60f4-44f0-9eea-ee05702a8a7b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d515d3d6-cc76-4aa7-a29e-5d3bec1c97ed","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08abe0c37f20c6b8","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011FYdLoGwKL3V2itd52qjS3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015VrfR6KE8CuZT5PXkWz5Z6","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html","prompt":"Find guidance about lb_tree_search, extra_subsolvers, lower bound improvement, MIP-style tree search, and when users should manually enable lb_tree_search via subsolver_params or extra_subsolvers. Quote specific recommendations."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1320,"cache_read_input_tokens":28199,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1320,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":43,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyBKtYZrmRZtzSNNqjb","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"09cd0284-875a-40c7-ad76-be909d11d9b5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:13.267Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"09cd0284-875a-40c7-ad76-be909d11d9b5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08abe0c37f20c6b8","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011FYdLoGwKL3V2itd52qjS3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L9vhNMSTV9jpTskivUaKdM","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CP-SAT \"lb_tree_search\" Achterberg \"best-first search\" lower bound LP relaxation paper"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1320,"cache_read_input_tokens":28199,"output_tokens":278,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1320},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":278,"cache_read_input_tokens":28199,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1320,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1320,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyBKtYZrmRZtzSNNqjb","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"20d0028e-0773-4cde-a5fe-ff7687b0e386","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:13.787Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"09cd0284-875a-40c7-ad76-be909d11d9b5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a08abe0c37f20c6b8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015VrfR6KE8CuZT5PXkWz5Z6","type":"tool_result","content":"# Guidance on lb_tree_search and Lower Bound Improvement\n\n## What is lb_tree_search?\n\nThe `lb_tree_search` subsolver is a full problem subsolver that prioritizes improving proven bounds rather than finding better solutions. According to the documentation: \"This solver is focussed on improving the proven bound, not on finding better solutions. By disproving the feasibility of the cheapest nodes in the search tree, it incrementally improves the bound, but has only little chances to find better solutions.\"\n\n## When to Enable lb_tree_search\n\nThe guide recommends manually enabling this subsolver when:\n\n1. **You're struggling with bound quality** - If your solver finds reasonable solutions quickly but struggles to prove their optimality, this strategy can help incrementally tighten the lower bound.\n\n2. **Through custom subsolver configuration** - You can add it via `subsolver_params` and activate it through `extra_subsolvers`:\n\n```python\nsolver.parameters.extra_subsolvers.append(\"lb_tree_search\")\n```\n\n## Key Recommendation\n\nThe primer emphasizes: \"For this example, it seems that the no_lp strategies are the most successful.\" This suggests that strategy selection depends on your specific problem. The guidance advises against indiscriminate parameter tweaking, cautioning that \"tampering with them could disrupt optimizations.\"\n\n**Bottom line**: Enable `lb_tree_search` only when you have evidence from solver logs that bound improvement is your bottleneck, not solution quality."}]},"uuid":"63dfd6e4-13bd-4332-ace3-0aadbeb5833b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:18.245Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"09cd0284-875a-40c7-ad76-be909d11d9b5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"20d0028e-0773-4cde-a5fe-ff7687b0e386","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"a08abe0c37f20c6b8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L9vhNMSTV9jpTskivUaKdM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT \"lb_tree_search\" Achterberg \"best-first search\" lower bound LP relaxation paper\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Math. Prog. Comp. (2009) 1:1–41 DOI 10.1007/s12532-008-0001-1 FULL LENGTH PAPER\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Tobias-Achterberg/publication/225664381_SCIP_Solving_constraint_integer_programs/links/00b495295d5c15acb5000000/SCIP-Solving-constraint-integer-programs.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A Constraint Integer Programming Approach for Resource- ...\",\"url\":\"https://d-nb.info/1248218094/34\"},{\"title\":\"Learning to Run Heuristics in Tree Search\",\"url\":\"https://www.ijcai.org/proceedings/2017/0092.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Branch-and-bound algorithms: A survey of recent advances in searching, branching, and pruning - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1572528616000062\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Relaxation-Aware Heuristics for Exact Optimization in Graphical Models | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-58942-4_31\"},{\"title\":\"US8463729B2 - LP relaxation modification and cut selection in a MIP solver - Google Patents\",\"url\":\"https://patents.google.com/patent/US8463729B2/en\"},{\"title\":\"A study of tighter lower bounds in LP relaxation based placement | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220904406_A_study_of_tighter_lower_bounds_in_LP_relaxation_based_placement\"},{\"title\":\"Domain reduction techniques for global NLP and MINLP ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1706.08601\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about CP-SAT, Achterberg's work, and lower bound techniques in tree search. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Key Information Found\n\nSCIP combines the CP, SAT, and MIP techniques on a very low level, with all involved algorithms operating on a single search tree, which is foundational work by Achterberg on constraint integer programming.\n\nMIP components can base their heuristic decisions on statistics gathered by CP algorithms or vice versa, and both can use the dual information provided by the LP relaxation of the current subproblem, demonstrating how lower bounds from LP relaxations are integrated into tree search.\n\nThe LP relaxation of an MIP is obtained by dropping the integrality restrictions of the variables, and it can be solved efficiently to provide a dual bound on the objective value which can be used for the bounding step in branch-and-bound.\n\nRegarding best-first search strategies, if the lower bound is strongly correlated with the subproblem objective values, this measure-of-best will encourage exploration of subproblems with better solutions, though in practice lower bounds may not be a good proxy for the objective function value.\n\nThe search results reference Achterberg's work on SCIP, though the specific \"lb_tree_search\" function and the detailed paper on best-first search strategies with lower bound LP relaxation were not directly located in these results. You may want to search directly for Achterberg's SCIP publication or the CP-SAT solver documentation for more specific technical details on those implementations.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a1465d50-7efc-4ca3-9723-f19addd89156","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:07:25.092Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"20d0028e-0773-4cde-a5fe-ff7687b0e386","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a1465d50-7efc-4ca3-9723-f19addd89156","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08abe0c37f20c6b8","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01CtGm2LpTE4J21zfYQN8qkj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"已经有足够信息整合一份精炼调研。我们项目背景是 70x70 网格、Benders 分解、需要证明 UNSAT 来收紧上界，正好是 lb_tree_search 的目标场景。\n\n# CP-SAT lb_tree_search 深度调研\n\n## 1. 算法本质：MIP 风格的\"全树保留\"分支搜索\n\n`lb_tree_search` 不是 LCG（懒子句生成），而是更接近**经典 MIP 分支定界**：\n\n- **关键区别**：CP-SAT 默认 SAT 风格搜索是\"深度优先 + 学到冲突就回跳\"，开放节点不显式保留；而 lb_tree_search **保留整棵已展开的树**。\n- **下界报告机制**：proto 注释原话——\"Keeping the whole tree allow us to report a better objective lower bound coming from the **worst open node** in the tree\"。也就是说，当前全局下界 = 所有未关闭叶子里最低的 LP 松弛值。这是 MIP 求解器（SCIP/CPLEX/Gurobi）的标准做法。\n- **配合 LP**：默认会把 `root_lp_iterations` 调到 100,000，强烈依赖单纯形求解松弛。可选 `save_lp_basis_in_lb_tree_search` 在节点间复用 LP basis（实验性，cuts/化简变化时不稳）。\n- **跟 LCG/lb_relax_lns 的分工**：LCG 是子句驱动的可行性证明；`use_lb_relax_lns`（默认 true，>=16 worker 才启用）是用 LNS 邻域反向证下界。lb_tree_search 走的是第三条路——**用结构化 best-first 树搜索关掉廉价节点来逐步抬升下界**。\n\n## 2. 启用条件 / 阈值（来自 cp_model_search.cc）\n\n- **默认行为**：当用户没指定 subsolvers 列表时，`names.push_back(\"lb_tree_search\")` **无条件加入候选名单**（不像 lb_relax_lns 有 16 worker 阈值）。\n- **必要前提**：\n  - 必须有 objective。无目标问题里它会被 `if (params.optimize_with_lb_tree_search()) continue;` 过滤。\n  - **不能在 `interleave_search`（确定性单线程交错模式）下运行**——明确被跳过。\n- **实际占位**：每个 worker slot 一个 subsolver，名单里有它就分一个线程。8 worker 的默认门户里通常会分到 1 个。\n\n## 3. 关键 proto 字段（stable 分支 sat_parameters.proto）\n\n| 字段 | 行号 | 默认 | 说明 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `optimize_with_lb_tree_search` | 2078 | **false** | 单 subsolver 开关；门户里通过 subsolver_params 的副本设 true |\n| `save_lp_basis_in_lb_tree_search` | 2083 | false | 实验性，跨节点复用 LP basis |\n| `share_objective_bounds` | — | true | lb_tree_search 副本里**强制设 false**，避免被其他 worker 拉高的上界污染下界证明 |\n| `root_lp_iterations` | — | 默认低 | lb_tree_search 副本里设 100,000 |\n| `extra_subsolvers` | — | [] | 用户手动追加 `\"lb_tree_search\"` 强制启用 |\n| `subsolver_params` | — | [] | 用户自定义副本参数 |\n\n## 4. 学术依据\n\n没有\"lb_tree_search\"专题论文，但血统清晰：\n- **Achterberg 的 SCIP**（Math. Prog. Comp. 2009）：constraint integer programming 把 CP/SAT/MIP 放在同一棵树上，dual bound 来自 LP 松弛，best-first 节点选择基于开放节点最低 LP 值。\n- **Branch-and-bound 综述**（Morrison et al., Discrete Optim. 2016）：best-first / best-bound 节点选择是改善下界的标配。\n- Perron 的 OR-Tools CP-SAT 公开演讲（CMU EWO）里多次说门户里**故意放一个\"看着像 MIP\"的 worker** 专门盯下界，就是 lb_tree_search。\n\n## 5. 我们项目应该怎么用\n\n**适用性诊断**：Phase 3B 全规模证明里，外层 `outer_search` 加 Benders 的痛点确实是**证 UNSAT / 收紧 area 上界**——下界提升慢、`best_bound` 卡住——正是 lb_tree_search 的目标。但有几个坑：\n\n1. **master 是纯 0/1 + 大量 reified 几何约束**，LP 松弛信息量本来就弱（OR-Tools 的 linearization_level=2 也只覆盖一部分），lb_tree_search 的边际收益会比经典 MIP 小。建议先对单个 candidate area 在 Benders **binding 子问题**（更接近 MIP）开它，master 不要单独开。\n2. **不要在 `interleave_search=true` 时开**。我们 `exact_parallel_scheduler.py` 里如果走的是确定性 interleave，会被静默跳过，白占名额。\n3. **shared bound 关闭副作用**：lb_tree_search 副本不接收其他 worker 的目标上界，所以**不能在 worker 数 ≤ 4 时让它独占**——只有上界并发推进时下界证明才有意义。我们 `--parallel-processes 4` 的场景，开 lb_tree_search 等于砍掉 1/4 算力。建议**仅当 `--parallel-processes >= 8` 时启用**。\n4. **per-process worker（CP-SAT 内部 num_workers）≥ 8 才值得**。我们外层多进程 + 每进程 CP-SAT，外层 4 进程 × 内层 8 worker 才到 32，那时候 lb_tree_search 默认就在内层名单里了，不需要额外动作。\n\n### 具体配置建议\n\n```python\n# src/models/binding_subproblem.py 或 master_model.py 的 CP-SAT 求解器创建处\nsolver = cp_model.CpSolver()\np = solver.parameters\n\n# 前提：本进程内部 worker 数充足（>=8），且非 interleave 模式\nif p.num_search_workers >= 8 and not p.interleave_search:\n    # 不要直接置顶 optimize_with_lb_tree_search=true（会让所有 worker 都跑这套）\n    # 正确做法是追加一个专门的 subsolver 副本\n    p.extra_subsolvers.append(\"lb_tree_search_aggressive\")\n    sp = p.subsolver_params.add()\n    sp.name = \"lb_tree_search_aggressive\"\n    sp.optimize_with_lb_tree_search = True\n    sp.share_objective_bounds = False        # 必须 False，否则下界证明被污染\n    sp.root_lp_iterations = 100000\n    sp.linearization_level = 2               # 强 LP 松弛\n    # save_lp_basis_in_lb_tree_search = True  # 实验性，先不开，稳定后再试\n\n# 如果是 4 worker 的小 budget（包括我们 outer_search 的当前默认）：\n# 不要手动启用 lb_tree_search，会牺牲找解的并行度\n```\n\n**Phase 3B Lane B（确定性调优）建议**：在 S6 的 stage-specific worker matrix 里，**只对 binding 子问题、且 num_workers≥8 的 profile** 加 lb_tree_search 副本；master/routing 阶段保持默认。配合 D 通道 runtime 诊断，记录 `best_bound` 提升曲线归因到哪个 subsolver（CP-SAT log 里 `[lb_tree_search]` 标签），**有数据才落到 r20260416 之后的 production 配置**。AI sidecar (Lane C) 不能直接改这个开关——属于 proof-relevant 配置，必须走 Lane B 的确定性实验。\n\nSources:\n- [or-tools sat_parameters.proto (stable)](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto)\n- [CP-SAT Primer — Parameters](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html)\n- [CP-SAT Primer — Under the Hood](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html)\n- [Perron — CP-SAT and OR-Tools (CMU EWO)](https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf)\n- [Achterberg — SCIP: Solving Constraint Integer Programs](https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Tobias-Achterberg/publication/225664381_SCIP_Solving_constraint_integer_programs/links/00b495295d5c15acb5000000/SCIP-Solving-constraint-integer-programs.pdf)\n- [Morrison et al. — Branch-and-bound algorithms survey](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1572528616000062)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2179,"cache_read_input_tokens":29519,"output_tokens":3191,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2179},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3191,"cache_read_input_tokens":29519,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2179,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2179,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyCmQjjPTaFqf5JHDDy","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b6f38d08-77cb-49f9-aa3d-4a27f287fd85","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:08:22.166Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
